			"author": {
				"name": "Katerina Marchán",
				"url": "https://toot.cat/@zkat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-06T19:21:51.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://alpha.polymaths.social/@roguefoam\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>roguefoam</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ollicle\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ollicle</span></a></span> the biggest challenge for anyone trying to replace yaml with KDL is that KDL isn't a JSON-style data representation format. It's node-based, like XML, so you need to handle your data a little differently</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
